{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://docs.oasis-open.org/sarif/sarif/v2.1.0/errata01/os/schemas/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "grype",
          "version": "0.118.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/anchore/grype",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "CVE-2023-31486-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2023-31486 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "HTTP::Tiny before 0.083, a Perl core module since 5.13.9 and available standalone on CPAN, has an insecure default TLS configuration where users must opt in to verify certificates."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2023-31486",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2023-31486\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.34.0-3ubuntu1.9\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2023-31486](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2023-31486)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2023-31486**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.34.0-3ubuntu1.9  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04  | [CVE-2023-31486](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2023-31486)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.34.0-3ubuntu1.9?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-22.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2022-4899-libzstd1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2022-4899 low vulnerability for libzstd1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A vulnerability was found in zstd v1.4.10, where an attacker can supply empty string as an argument to the command line tool to cause buffer overrun."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2022-4899",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2022-4899\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libzstd1\nVersion: 1.4.8+dfsg-3build1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2022-4899](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2022-4899)",
