            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-42497-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-42497 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Archive::Tar versions before 3.08 for Perl extract hardlinks to attacker controlled paths outside the extraction directory.\n\n_make_special_file() passes the tar header's linkname to link() without validating it against absolute paths or .. segments, creating a hardlink that shares the victim file's inode.\n\nA subsequent write through the extracted name modifies the victim file, and the post-extraction chmod, chown, and utime block in _extract_file() (guarded only against symlinks via -l) applies the tar header's mode, owner, and timestamps to the shared inode during extraction alone."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-42497",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-42497\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.34.0-3ubuntu1.9\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-42497](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-42497)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-42497**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.34.0-3ubuntu1.9  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04  | [CVE-2026-42497](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-42497)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.34.0-3ubuntu1.9?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-22.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80230-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-80230 medium vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When `CURLOPT_PINNEDPUBLICKEY` is configured alongside options that disable\nstandard peer verification (`CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER = 0` and\n`CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYHOST = 0`), libcurl fails to enforce public key pinning on\nconnections established without a presented server certificate. Bypassing the\npinning check under these disabled-verification conditions allows\nunauthenticated connections to succeed when they should be rejected."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-80230",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-80230\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 7.81.0-1ubuntu1.27\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-80230](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-80230)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-80230**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | curl  | 7.81.0-1ubuntu1.27  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04  | [CVE-2026-80230](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-80230)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/curl@7.81.0-1ubuntu1.27?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-22.04"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-80230-libcurl4",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-80230 medium vulnerability for libcurl4 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When `CURLOPT_PINNEDPUBLICKEY` is configured alongside options that disable\nstandard peer verification (`CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYPEER = 0` and\n`CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYHOST = 0`), libcurl fails to enforce public key pinning on\nconnections established without a presented server certificate. Bypassing the\npinning check under these disabled-verification conditions allows\nunauthenticated connections to succeed when they should be rejected."
              },
