            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-48959-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-48959 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "IO::Uncompress::Unzip versions before 2.220 for Perl allow CPU exhaustion via per-byte read loop in fastForward.\n\nfastForward() compares length $offset (the digit count of the offset, 1 to 19) against the chunk size $c instead of $offset itself, so $c shrinks from 16 KiB to 1-19 bytes per iteration.\n\nExtracting a named entry from an attacker supplied zip via IO::Uncompress::Unzip-\u003enew($zip, Name =\u003e $target) drives a per-byte read loop scaling with the entry's compressed size, up to the non-Zip64 4 GiB cap."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-48959",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-48959\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.34.0-3ubuntu1.9\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-48959](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-48959)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-48959**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.34.0-3ubuntu1.9  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04  | [CVE-2026-48959](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-48959)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/perl-base@5.34.0-3ubuntu1.9?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-22.04\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.5"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-86145-libpcre2-8-0",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-86145 medium vulnerability for libpcre2-8-0 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "PCRE2 before 10.48 allows a pcre2_dfa_match out-of-bounds write because reuse of a cached workspace block, in a recursive DFA matching workspace, lacks a size check (even though a newly allocated block, for the same purpose, does have a size check). This outcome requires an attacker-controlled regular expression, or a recursive pattern in conjunction with a small heap limit (this can be set through the API)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-86145",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-86145\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libpcre2-8-0\nVersion: 10.39-3ubuntu0.1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-86145](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-86145)",
