              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The X-mount.subdir option uses a detached-tree fast path on Linux 6.15 and later and passes the configured subdirectory to open_tree() with AT_SYMLINK_NOFOLLOW. That flag does not stop intermediate symlink traversal or keep resolution inside the newly mounted filesystem. A local unprivileged user with an fstab-authorized X-mount.subdir entry can attach a host path at the intended mountpoint."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-78409",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-78409\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: mount\nVersion: 2.37.2-4ubuntu3.6\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-78409](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-78409)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-78409**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | mount  | 2.37.2-4ubuntu3.6  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04  | [CVE-2026-78409](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-78409)  |\n"
              },
