            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-54370-libacl1",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-54370 medium vulnerability for libacl1 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "acl before version 2.4.0 contains a time-of-check to time-of-use (TOCTOU) race condition vulnerability that allows local attackers to escalate privileges by replacing a pathname component with a symbolic link between an lstat() check and subsequent symlink-following operations such as stat(), chown(), chmod(), acl_get_file(), and acl_set_file(). Attackers who control a pathname component can redirect file access control list operations to arbitrary files when getfacl, setfacl, or chacl is invoked by a privileged process over an attacker-controlled path, resulting in local privilege escalation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-54370",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-54370\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: libacl1\nVersion: 2.3.1-1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-54370](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-54370)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-54370**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | libacl1  | 2.3.1-1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04  | [CVE-2026-54370](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-54370)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/ubuntu/libacl1@2.3.1-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=ubuntu-22.04\u0026upstream=acl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "7.2"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-18477-tar",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-18477 medium vulnerability for tar package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A TOCTOU (Time-of-Check Time-of-Use) vulnerability in GNU tar's incremental dumpdir 'X' rename handling allows a local attacker with write access to a directory being backed up to influence the restore process if the attacker has access to the system where the restore is being performed. During restoration, files or directories may be created, renamed or overwritten outside the intended extraction directory. This could lead to unauthorized file modification or, in some cases, privilege escalation. Exploitation does not require the attacker to modify or craft the archive, and standard backup and restore workflows—including extracting into a newly created directory without using the -P option do not mitigate the issue."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-18477",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-18477\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: tar\nVersion: 1.34+dfsg-1ubuntu0.1.22.04.6\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04\nLink: [CVE-2026-18477](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-18477)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-18477**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | tar  | 1.34+dfsg-1ubuntu0.1.22.04.6  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | ubuntu:distro:ubuntu:22.04  | [CVE-2026-18477](https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2026-18477)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
